    "description": "Antique Frank M. Whiting & Company Sterling silver covered sugar bowl, weighing approximately 433 grams including its fitted lid. The reeded melon-form body is extensively hand-chased with floral and foliate decoration and raised on a pedestal base, with ornate double handles and a coordinating lid and finial. The underside is marked Frank M. Whiting & Company, Sterling, Hand Chased and No. 640. The No. 640 identification is independently supported by a documented Frank M. Whiting five-piece service that specifically includes a covered sugar and describes the pieces as reeded melon form, hand-chased with floral designs and marked #640. (Charlton Hall Auctions)\n\nVery good condition with no dents or dings and age-appropriate surface wear. Approximately 433g. See photos for dimensions, marks, details and condition.",
